display selected identifier's references

Usage:
  gopls [flags] references [references-flags] <target>

Example:
	$ gopls references -pkg go/ast Decl
	$ gopls references golang.org/x/tools/go/ast/inspector.Cursor

references-flags:
  -context=int
    	number of lines of surrounding code context to print around each reference (inclusive of ref line, so 1 prints just the ref line)
  -d,-declaration
    	include the declaration of the specified identifier in the results
  -json
    	emit output in JSON format
  -limit=int
    	maximum number of results to return (0 means no limit)
  -pkg=string
    	scopes the query to a specific package, resolving ambiguities in versioned package paths (for example, gopkg.in/yaml.v3) or vanity domains.
  -pos=location
    	targets a file span. Format: file.go[:lineStart[:colStart]-lineEnd[:colEnd]], file.go[:line:colStart-colEnd], or file.go[:#offsetStart-#offsetEnd] (1-based line, 1-based column in UTF-8 bytes, 0-based byte offset). Also accepts a single point, returning a location that has that point as both the start and end.
